WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.309 --> 00:00:02.700
(crowd clapping) Oh, miss Harlow.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.250
Oh, my goodness.
Thank you for having me.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:09.770
Oh, I'm so very honored and excited to meet you.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.910
So nice to meet you as well.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.120
Okay.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.060
Let's go right to your childhood Winnie.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.200
Okay, let's start from the beginning.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.890
Let's start from the beginning.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.980
Okay, when you were four you were diagnosed

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.500
with an auto-immune condition, vitiligo.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.140
And what was your life like when you were a kid?

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.390
What was your family like?

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.800
What were your feelings?

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.220
Who were you at four years old?

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.210
At four years old, I was a really happy child.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.120
And I think that's because my family was

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.920
so loving and so supporting.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:47.920
And so, they had such a will to make sure that I felt normal

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:54.380
and felt like my differences were

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.150
a very important part of who I was.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:01.470
When I did first get vitiligo my mom was, she was worried,

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.290
you know, it was something that she hadn't heard of before.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:07.620
So I remember her bringing me over to my grandmother

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.500
and my aunt and lifting up the back of my shirt

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.660
and being like, look, there's a new spot on her back.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:15.070
And my grandmother was like, you can't do that to her

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:17.110
because she's going to feel like her differences

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.610
are something that's negative and that's not right.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:22.560
She has to grow up knowing that all the things

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.050
that make her her are valid and are beautiful.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:29.490
And that's how you make her feel important.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.940
Well, I love hearing that too, because I,

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.460
as a parent am learning on the job,

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.160
I think we probably all are.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.180
And what a blessing

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:42.720
that your grandmother had such awesome wisdom for your mom.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.050
For sure, it's so important I think today,

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:48.730
especially with social media and so many outlets for kids to

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:52.130
go to, to learn or watch things,

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:55.010
I think we forget that the most important place

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.450
for children to learn is at home.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.030
What parents teach their kids

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.850
and enforce in their kids is so important.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:06.500
Well, you've been a real force on social media.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.470
And ironically, I heard you were sort of, you know,

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:12.680
tentative to put yourself out there at first.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:17.330
And now you're one of the world's biggest supermodels.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:20.160
How does it go from like tentative putting toe in

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.900
the water to being one of the most famous beauties

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.590
on planet earth?

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:27.470
Stop. (laughing)

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:28.303
It's true.

00:02:28.303 --> 00:02:30.680
Thank you, I appreciate it.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.900
I think it was just because it was something that was new

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:35.470
and anything that's new is kind of scary.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:39.560
But when I realized that people were so excited

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:43.610
about me putting myself out there and the way I felt

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.160
about myself, and how I felt like I was beautiful

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.380
and I wasn't going

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.450
to let someone else's opinions get me down and

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.300
that encourage others to do the same,

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.770
I was like, you know what, if it's inspiring

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.930
for other people, let me continue.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.610
Let me just be out there

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.680
because everyone goes through something.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.850
Everyone is different which is

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.390
what makes us all at the same.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.040
So, I have this thing where like,

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.710
people always wanna be normal, but like,

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:09.700
what is normal?

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:13.730
There's this idea of what normal is, but everyone's normal.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.090
You have freckles, that's normal.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.440
You have brown hair, that's normal.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.810
You have green eyes, that's normal.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.430
You have brown eyes, that's normal.

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:20.943
All these things are normal.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.010
I mean, do you wanna have kids?

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.698
Because I think you should be basically a parent to us all.

00:03:27.698 --> 00:03:29.040
(laughing)

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.830
I do want kids, but not right now. (laughing)

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:35.190
I mean, I think that when you talk

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:39.250
about how we all have this shared common experience,

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:43.680
to hear you talking about that, I think I just,

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.473
I look forward to my daughters, you know, learning

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:54.510
and experiencing life through your eyes and your wisdom,

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:59.650
and your words because I think they're very calming

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:03.230
and healing, and yet really inspiring and energizing

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.160
at the same time
Thank you.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:09.230
I think that's because I don't take myself too seriously

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.500
and I understand that I'm a human like,

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.290
I always say, I don't believe in role models.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:17.660
I don't believe in putting anyone on a pedestal to say,

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.290
this is who I should be like,

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:23.370
but I do believe in pulling inspiration from everyone.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.430
No, one's perfect.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.020
People are going to make mistakes.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:27.670
I make mistakes all the time.

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:30.610
And while I love that people pull inspiration for me,

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:35.120
I wouldn't wanna be anyone's like, role model

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.473
or put up on a pedestal because I know I'm only human.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:41.380
I don't know Winnie,

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.800
I'm getting super hero vibes.(laughing)

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.780
I'm hearing superhero wisdom and--

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:50.140
Even superheroes have their kryptonite.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.930
Yes, they absolutely do.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:55.120
In fact, superheroes are incredibly flawed.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.840
I'm trying to think inside, like what my kryptonite is.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.203
Do you have a kryptonite?

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:04.960
My kryptonite is maybe like, I'm from the hood

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.290
so sometimes I just like to get like real street with it

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:09.410
and just say, what's real and what's on my mind.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.540
Sometimes I need a little filter sometimes.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:15.763
So yeah, not having a filter sometimes is my kryptonite.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.370
I like your kryptonite, I'm into your kryptonite.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.500
I feel like I want, like, I want more

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.670
of your street no filter.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.920
I'm already rocking the body language of it

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.480
and I'd like to hear what comes out.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:35.030
I'm not going to lie, maybe we can throw down sometime

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:37.670
because I'm like, oh, I want in, I want some of like,

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.030
Winnie's no filter.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:42.780
Yeah, come to a party with me and we'll vibe out.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.965
Wow, Winnie you are making me feel alive again.

00:05:45.965 --> 00:05:47.650
(laughing)

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:50.355
I used to go to parties.

00:05:50.355 --> 00:05:51.190
For sure.
Winnie,

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:53.120
will you please take me to a party?

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.360
I have been in my mom mode,
100%

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.370
For so long, like--

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.160
Listen, and then When I finally have kids,

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.750
then you can help me out there as well

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.470
cause I know I'm gonna need tons of help.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:04.210
Yes, I can.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.950
And I too will always be encouraging

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:10.070
for us to not take ourselves too seriously,

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.190
for us to promote strength

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:15.139
and humor and humanity.
Yes.

00:06:15.139 --> 00:06:17.722
(upbeat music)

